title: tag:add
tags: [[GUI command]] [[Customising the GUI]]
kind: reference
summary: Add a tag to the selected metarecord

`tag:add <tag|negative_tag|mixed_tag> <tag>` gives the selected metarecord a tag, denies it, or marks it mixed, the field naming the answer: it answers `add`, `deny` or `mixed` through `mf.tag.answer` ([[The metafolder API]]), so the rules of [[Tag subsumption]] hold, and a path that names no tag yet creates it. The completion offers the paths of the existing tags. The keys are `, a t`, `, a n` and `, a m` ([[Tagging from the GUI]]). Written in the shipped `commands.js`, where its questions and what it runs can be edited ([[User commands]]).
